### 1.4 UNIVERSITIES & PROGRAMS

#### **40 Participating Universities:**

**Major Research Universities:**
- Sapienza University of Rome
- University of Milan (Bicocca, Bocconi, Politecnico)
- University of Bologna
- University of Padua
- University of Turin (Politecnico)
- University of Florence
- University of Naples

**Regional Universities:**
- Across all major Italian regions (North, Central, South, Islands)
- Mix of public and private institutions
- Politechnic, research, and specialized universities

#### **Course Offerings:**
- **432 total courses** across 40 universities
- **Master's degree programs** (Second Cycle)
- Fields: Engineering, Business, Law, Medicine, Humanities, Sciences, Technology
- Available from March 2, 2026 (most; some later)
- Searchable course database on website

#### **What Students Get:**
- Tuition fee exemption (full waiver)
- Monthly study grant/stipend for living expenses
- Plane ticket assistance
- Visa and residence permit-related expenses covered
- Accommodation support (varies by university)
- Health insurance
- Academic and psychosocial support (varies)

---

### 1.5 PARTNERS & SUPPORT NETWORK

#### **National Partners:**
- **UNHCR Italy** – Overall program coordination, refugee status verification
- **Italian Ministry of Foreign Affairs & International Cooperation** – Policy support
- **Caritas Italiana** – Housing, integration, community support
- **Diaconia Valdese** – Mental health, psychosocial support
- **Centro Astalli** – Legal support, documentation assistance
- **Other partner organizations** – Varies by location

#### **Local Partner Services (by university/city):**
- Housing coordination and accommodation
- Reception and integration activities
- Mental health and psychosocial support
- Legal guidance and documentation help
- Healthcare access
- Community connection and events
- Emergency support

---

### 1.6 FAQ SECTION CONTENT (Current)

#### **20+ Questions Covered:**

**Application Process (7 questions):**
- Where do I start?
- Can I create multiple profiles? (NO – explicitly forbidden)
- How can I apply?
- Who is eligible?
- What are basic requirements?
- How many applications can I submit? (Maximum 2 universities)
- What if I'm missing documentation?

**Scholarship & Benefits (5 questions):**
- What are the benefits?
- Is a fee required? (NO – participation is free)
- Can I receive multiple scholarships? (NO)
- English language requirement clarification
- What happens after graduation?

**Work & Study (2 questions):**
- Am I allowed to work? (YES – part-time, max 20 hrs/week)
- Is attendance mandatory? (Depends on program)

**Results & Timelines (3 questions):**
- When is the deadline? When will I get results?
- How can I follow my application progress? (Dashboard status tracking)
- When will courses start? (September/October 2026)

**Post-Graduation (2 questions):**
- Can I defer my admission? (NO)
- Can I request resettlement to another EU country? (NO – no resettlement program from Italy)

**Application Tracking:**
- Dashboard shows status: "Screening pending," "Refugee status confirmed," "Refugee status denied"
- UNHCR verification step tracked in dashboard
- Universities handle shortlisting, interviews, final selection
- Results communicated only via email

