## SECTION 6: INTEGRATION RECOMMENDATIONS

### How New Student Portal Complements Official Site

#### **Architecture Integration:**

**Option A: Separate but Linked (Recommended)**
```
universitycorridors.unhcr.it
├── [HOME] ← Link to → Support Portal (new site)
├── Admission
├── Universities ← Links to → Program details in Support Portal
├── FAQ ← Links to → Comprehensive FAQ in Support Portal
└── [Login/Register] ← Links to → Student Dashboard in Support Portal

Support Portal (new)
├── Student Dashboard (personal, login-required)
├── Resources Hub (public)
├── Blog & News (public)
├── FAQ (public & interactive)
├── Buddy Program (public info, login for coordination)
└── Alumni Network (semi-public, login for details)
```

**Advantages:**
- Main site remains focused on application process
- Support portal is specialized for student needs
- Clean separation of concerns
- Easy to navigate for different audiences
- Both discoverable from either site

**Option B: Unified Platform (Future)**
```
universitycorridors.unhcr.it (expanded)
├── Application Hub
├── Program Information
├── Student Dashboard (after admission)
├── Support Resources
├── Alumni Network
└── Career Services
```

---

#### **Data & Information Integration:**

**Real-Time Synchronization Needed:**
1. **University Information**
   - Pull university contact info from main site database
   - Link to course pages
   - Update coordinator/department contacts

2. **Scholarship & Financial Data**
   - Synchronize eligibility criteria
   - Share scholarship information
   - Link to hardship fund policies

3. **Partner Organization Info**
   - Pull partner contacts and services
   - Link to mental health, legal, housing resources
   - Update service descriptions

**Recommended Technical Approach:**
- API connection between sites (if possible)
- Regular data exports/imports
- Shared user database for login (single sign-on ideal)
- Centralized privacy/GDPR compliance system

